{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/772557-ex3-designing-dragonblooded-antagonists","id":772557,"title":"[Ex3] Designing Dragonblooded Antagonists?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-23T15:19:48-08:00","id":772557,"title":"[Ex3] Designing Dragonblooded Antagonists?","content":"Hey, I am running a pirate game set in the west and I plan for The Realm / Dragon-Blooded to feature prominently. While we wait for the Dragonblooded book, does anyone have any good design philosophies for making dragonblooded antagonists? In fights and out of fights? I do not have a good handle on what they should be able to do. I do plan on having a lot of sorcerers and martial artists to fill the ranks, but I'd like to have actual Dragon Blooded themed things too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T23:38:44-08:00","id":772849,"title":"","content":"Well, to start, did you play Dragonblood in 2nd ed? I just want to see what your own base is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T03:53:01-08:00","id":772917,"title":"","content":"I'd focus on the Peleps. They have elaborate navies of both the military and trade persuasion. You could easily have a smaller part of the house deciding to carve out their own niche in the West where no one will know they are pillaging resources and conscirpting men. Well, no one except the heroes whose island they decided to take <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Cue bribed gods helping the Peleps, the neighbouring kingdom that wants to take over the land, a gaggle of pirates used to pillaging and raping accross the island and a mysterious ghost ship and you have yourself a lovely set of antagonists for the PC's to sort through <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T05:56:44-08:00","id":773022,"title":"","content":"The Terrestrial keyword gives some insights into Dragon-Blooded limitations that you can keep in mind when working with Solar charms as a base.<br /> The most consistent ones I've noticed are-<br /> Extra-Action charms (including counterattacks and reflexive clashes) don't come easily to them. If you want to whittle down a superior opponent you bring friends.<br /> Decisive attacks are supposed to hurt them. It seems a group of Dragon-Blooded is going to want someone who can take a hit and force an initiative reset for their allies to exploit rather than shrug off the mightiest of blows.<br /> <br /> I suspect anima levels are going to be a frequent cost associated with Dragon-Blooded charms. It's very thematic to have them let loose with their anima flux the first chance they get.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T07:49:59-08:00","id":773107,"title":"","content":"I did not play Dragon-Blooded in 2e, though I do have Thousand Correct Actions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T07:54:35-08:00","id":773112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/772557-ex3-designing-dragonblooded-antagonists?p=773022#post773022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Terrestrial keyword gives some insights into Dragon-Blooded limitations that you can keep in mind when working with Solar charms as a base.<br /> The most consistent ones I've noticed are-<br /> Extra-Action charms (including counterattacks and reflexive clashes) don't come easily to them. If you want to whittle down a superior opponent you bring friends.<br /> Decisive attacks are supposed to hurt them. It seems a group of Dragon-Blooded is going to want someone who can take a hit and force an initiative reset for their allies to exploit rather than shrug off the mightiest of blows.<br /> <br /> I suspect anima levels are going to be a frequent cost associated with Dragon-Blooded charms. It's very thematic to have them let loose with their anima flux the first chance they get.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I think you are generally on point; they don't seem to have any issue with counter attacks-- (crane style) but they seem barred from reflexive clashes and any charm that allows for more than one attack besides a counterattack seems difficult. They also seem to be somewhat less mote efficient.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2116-jivex","name":"JiveX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2116_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T08:21:26-08:00","id":773139,"title":"","content":"I probably could've worded that better.<br /> Crane Form's counterattacks require full defence or defend other action so you forgo your regular attacks by taking advantage of that. The rule of thumb is that Dragon-Blooded are going to be making one attack per round unless they really let loose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T08:26:14-08:00","id":773142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/772557-ex3-designing-dragonblooded-antagonists?p=773139#post773139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I probably could've worded that better.<br /> Crane Form's counterattacks require full defence or defend other action so you forgo your regular attacks by taking advantage of that. The rule of thumb is that Dragon-Blooded are going to be making one attack per round unless they really let loose.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was actually think of the post form charm that lets them make counterattacks as a celestial but prevents them from adding to defense as effectively","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2116-jivex","name":"JiveX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2116_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T08:44:21-08:00","id":773158,"title":"","content":"Ah, Crossed Wings Denial. It's probably expensive and limited enough to make a counterattack restriction unnecessary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T08:57:09-08:00","id":773172,"title":"","content":"Crossed wing's Denial is Expensive, but its also arguably the best decisive counterattack charm out there (better than the solar action long one certainly because it doesn't consume your action). There are also several unrestricted counterattacks in MA which Terrestrials use with equal ease. Anyway, not a big deal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2116-jivex","name":"JiveX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2116_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T10:14:03-08:00","id":773228,"title":"","content":"I'd keep in mind that you're writing for NPCs, not PCs. Even if they're DBs and their charms should be weaker than Solars, I'd lean towards making the charms fairly powerful, to compensate both for their low number and to not make them pushovers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Some of me humble homebrew for ex3:<br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hOOjEGyoq3owLoUwIwTfWKTffzo_udsiUTwomw7wudA/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Artifacts for Crumple's DB homebrew</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1tI2T1Re0G8QOuoXkH7Y4PrKQxk1BPEGpbi82SpkTyIw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Some Lintha QCs</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1O2I_2iWTCflJ36ggkDvjTeXmzFsGHKRxAi6L_Ry6g4w/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A Wyld Behemoth</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8838-tds","name":"TDS","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T12:50:44-08:00","id":773350,"title":"","content":"The problem i have at the moment is, its very hard to guessimate the power level of the DB charms, especially how weak some of the solar charms are with 3rd ed (i am looking at you Food gathering exercise !!). One of my players wanted to have 2 DB Retainers, he payed 8 merit dots for them, wrote a very nice story for their backgrounds, but they don't have charms...they are not immaculates, obviously (lost eggs), one of them is stealthy assassin and other is a diplomat...<br /> <br /> I wish we had a few, like 2 charms per ability examples we can base our customs charms for DB.<br /> <br /> I guess we have to wait till fire has finished wroughting...until then i am trying to stick to giant lizards and zombies as antagonists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/910-ncolic","name":"Ncolic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T12:55:21-08:00","id":773355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JiveX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/772557-ex3-designing-dragonblooded-antagonists?p=773172#post773172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Crossed wing's Denial is Expensive, but its also arguably the best decisive counterattack charm out there (better than the solar action long one certainly because it doesn't consume your action). There are also several unrestricted counterattacks in MA which Terrestrials use with equal ease. Anyway, not a big deal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think if I had to write proper guidelines the spirit of the rule would be significantly interfering with action economy.<br /> A lot of the existing counterattack charms have enough of their own restrictions to not warrant an additional limitation with the Terrestrial keyword but I'd still advise that people keep an eye on how many attacks they're allowing Dragon-Blooded NPC to make in the same round.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}